  "chapter_rationale": "Chapter boundaries follow the playlist titles and descriptions. A chapter holds 1 to 4 consecutive content lectures (about 25 to 130 min), so that one author can hold the whole chapter in view. Lectures 1-4 form chapter 1 (accumulation functions, simple and compound interest, v and d, i against d). Lectures 6-9 split into nominal rates (6, 7) and the force of interest (8, 9). Lecture 10 (inflation) joins lecture 11 (equation of value) because both compare cash flows measured in different units. Annuities are split by the playlist: 16-19 (basic forms, pilot) 21-24 (perpetuities, continuous, deferred, unknowns) 26-29 (varying). Bonds (36-41) split at lecture 39 into pricing and amortization. Lectures 42-46 split into rate behaviour with risk structure (42-44) and the yield curve (45-46). Lectures 47-49 (general term structure) and 50-52 (duration) are single topics of 3 lectures.",
